---
mm: 1.2
kind: app
name: mcu-shell
option: buildable-host no
use: mm.shell.board
use: mm.shell.fs
use: mm.shell
use: mm.fs
use: mm.fs.local
file: main.cpp
---

# mcu-shell

Interactive embedded shell over the selected mm.stdio console: mm.shell.board
with the level-2 command pack, the blink and sample scripts, and the file
commands of mm.shell.fs over the board's own storage, which it mounts at
/data through mm.fs.local -- littlefs on the flash region on a Pico,
formatted the first time, and the device map's directory on Linux. A board
whose storage does not mount still gets the shell, with a line saying so; the
file commands then answer that nothing is there.

apps/mcu-shell-sd is the same shell with the board's SD card mounted at /sd
as well, for boards with a socket, at the cost of FatFs in the image.
